/benches/test_data
/code_packages
/drafts
# Trailing slash: directories only. Without it these are file globs too, and
# `/references*` silently swallowed a root `references.md` — plausible for a
# crate implementing a documented format. The `*` is kept so suffixed variants
# (`references_old/`, `trash2/`) are still caught.
/references*/
# Cargo build dirs, at any depth. Trailing slash = directories only; no leading
# slash = every level. This must not be `/target*`: that is anchored to the repo
# root, so a nested crate's build dir is missed (`fuzz/target/` only escaped
# because fuzz/.gitignore covers it separately), and being a file glob it also
# silently swallowed root files like `target_notes.md`.
target/
/trash*/
**/.cursor/

# Cargo.lock
*.bak
*.del
*.draft
*.errors

